{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The launcher loads the application's own config regardless of the caller's working directory and ignores an unrelated same-named relative config.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Launching from both /tmp and the conflicting other-directory returned the application's west/weekly configuration; direct comparisons confirmed the application config matched and the caller config was ignored, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d4c282026d6d4113","cmd-f2480a7d2d034d55","cmd-5299e29dbce34e3d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the existing configuration and business output in the application directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The application and both configuration files retained their baseline hashes, while successful launches continued to emit region=west and report=weekly before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-c93a544e8adc485f","cmd-d4c282026d6d4113","cmd-5299e29dbce34e3d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Propagate application errors to the launcher's caller instead of falsely reporting success.","status":"satisfied","summary":"During a bounded missing-config test, the application raised FileNotFoundError and the launcher returned exit code 1. The configuration was then restored and healthy output with exit code 0 was directly observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1b3a238f75b44e1"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Alpine Linux 3.23.3 and kernel 6.18.7-0-lts were unchanged. Python 3.12.15 was installed from the configured Alpine v3.23 repositories and remained functional after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7215ed53613c4f9c","cmd-4837082d18624dbc","cmd-cbc81cdd109d4d17","cmd-f2480a7d2d034d55","cmd-5299e29dbce34e3d","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: installing the required runtime, repairing the launcher, performing and restoring a bounded error test, and executing the mandatory restart protocol. The restart protocol was complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart application/data state, acknowledgement, a changed boot ID, and recovered application/data/platform state, corroborated by lifecycle boot observations. One minor unnecessary residue remained: cmd-7077bd53ebeb4e7c redirected reboot output to /tmp/executor-reboot.log, which was still present after execution rather than being cleaned up. No other unnecessary mutation was identified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cbc81cdd109d4d17","cmd-4855976d85704d9d","cmd-f1b3a238f75b44e1","cmd-f2480a7d2d034d55","cmd-7077bd53ebeb4e7c","cmd-da999173826a4038","cmd-5299e29dbce34e3d","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The launcher is working-directory independent, ignores the caller's conflicting config, preserves the original application data and output, propagates application failures, and survives a fully evidenced node restart without changing the OS release or kernel.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector could not inspect failed services because systemctl is unsupported on this Alpine node; this does not materially weaken verification of the on-demand report launcher.","A small executor-created reboot log remained under /tmp."]}
